**Critical bug confirmed:** `src/invoice.js:4` — the `subtotal()` loop was changed from `i < items.length` to `i < items.length - 1`, which silently drops the last line item from every invoice total. This is unrelated to the stated purpose of the commit ("Add percent discount") and breaks the existing test `subtotal adds every line`, plus `total()` transitively since it calls `subtotal()` via `discounted()`.

The new `discounted()`/`total(..., percent)` logic itself looks fine (floors the discount, clamps at zero, applied before tax). The fix is simply reverting the loop bound to `items.length`.

